.TH PDETEST 1
.SH NAME
pdetest \- test the five-point Laplacian
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B pdetest
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Pdetest
checks
.IR math (2)'s
.B lap5
against the Limbo stencil it replaced, which is kept inside the test as
the statement of what the operator is.
.PP
The interior of that kernel is easy and the border is not.
It exists so that the interior loop can run without a boundary test in
it, which means the edges are computed by separate code, once, for each
boundary condition.
Getting one of those wrong changes a handful of cells out of thousands
\(em invisible in a solve, and invisible in a convergence study.
So this compares every cell against the reference rather than checking
that a solve still looks reasonable.
.PP
All three boundary conditions are checked.
A solve run to try the thing out uses one of them and leaves the other
two unexercised, which is exactly what happened:
.B lap5
was measured on
.B clamp
alone and shipped before periodic and zero had ever been compared
against anything.
.PP
Grids one cell wide are checked too, in both directions, along with a
grid that is all border and no interior.
The border walk treats rows and columns separately and guards against
those cases, and the guards had never run.
.PP
One case does not use the reference at all: the discrete Laplacian of a
plane is zero everywhere inside, whatever the spacing.
That catches a sign or a spacing error which comparing against a
reference cannot, because a reference written from the same
misunderstanding would agree.
.SH SOURCE
.B /appl/cmd/pdetest.b
.SH SEE ALSO
.IR math-linalg (2),
.IR pde (2),
.IR sh-verify (1),
.IR sparsetest (1)
.SH BUGS
The comparison is a tolerance rather than an equality, because a C loop
may contract a multiply and an add into a fused one where Limbo does
not.
In practice the two agree exactly here, so the tolerance has never been
what let a run pass; removing the border walk, or exchanging
.I dx
for
.IR dy ,
makes it fail loudly, which is how that was established.
.PP
Only the stencil is tested.
Nothing here exercises
.IR pde (2)'s
time stepping, its solver plumbing, or the equations built on top \(em
.B wave
and
.B gray
have no test of their own.
.PP
Two dimensions only.
.IR amr (2)
uses a three-dimensional seven-point stencil, which shares none of this
code and has no test either.
